== casting 6 / AC-033, FR-024, FR-050, NFR-011: the roster rungs, and why this count is exact ==

  WHAT THIS COMMAND SELECTS. Both halves collect from ONE path,
  tests/test_protocol_prose.py. The 12 below is a grep count over a single
  node id; the figure under it is that whole module and nothing else. No peer
  module is in either selection. The 4 skipped are the rungs that need
  foundry-archive/ and forge-specs/, which are untracked and therefore absent
  from the detached worktree the sweep re-executes in -- they are the shape of
  a correct capture here, not a degraded one.

  WHY THIS PRINTS AN EXACT COUNT AND NOT A DERIVED VERDICT. The ruling is
  evidence/casting-1-no-degradation.log: the fragility is PEER-OWNERSHIP, not
  counting. tests/test_protocol_prose.py is casting 6s sole key_file in
  castings/manifest.json, so this population moves only when its owner moves
  it, and its owner recaptures in the same commit. Casting 1s derived-verdict
  and collected-floor shape is prescribed for a selection reaching a peer
  module; this one reaches none, and a floor here would cost real signal --
  730 and 700 both clear any floor worth setting, so a whole-module regression
  would still report MET. The two repairs casting 1 rejected on the record
  (declare the count volatile; select by explicit node id) are not reopened.

  THE DISCIPLINE THIS LOG AND ITS SEVEN SIBLINGS ARE HERE TO RECORD. All
  eight were staled at 17f2861, which added exactly one test to this module
  and did not recapture in the same commit. Every SELECTED count held; only
  the module total moved, by exactly one, in all eight. What the gate is
  asking for is therefore the recapture in the commit that moves the module --
  not a wider shape for a population no peer can move.

